{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said to Moses and to Aaron.</b> This pericha was stated before the one above it, concerning the plague of the firstborn — for this periclia was before the tenth of the month, from the new moon, while that of the plague of the firstborn was on the eve of Passover. But there is no earlier and later in the Torah; He did not wish to interrupt the sequence of the warning for all the plagues, and also wished to expound in order all the commandments dependent on the month of Nisan." "<b>In the land of Egypt.</b> Since this is a pericha of a commandment, it was necessary to specify where it was stated — just as we find with other commandments: some at Sinai, some in the Tent of Meeting, and some in the plains of Moab." "<b>לאמר.</b> Go and say to them immediately."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:02.107646821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}